{
  "title": "SYMFLUENCE: SYnergistic Modelling Framework for Linking and Unifying Earth-system Nexii for Computational Exploration",
  "description": "<p>SYMFLUENCE is a computational environmental modeling platform that streamlines the hydrological modeling workflow from domain setup through data acquisition, model execution, calibration, and evaluation. A four-tier layered architecture governed by typed component registries integrates hydrological models spanning multiple programming languages and modeling paradigms, unified through declarative YAML configuration with provenance captured by default.</p><p>Described and evaluated in the three-part paper series &quot;Out-standing in Every Field&quot;, &quot;The Registry as Social Contract&quot;, and &quot;From Configuration to Prediction&quot; (Eythorsson et al., 2026, Water Resources Research).</p>",
